<LegalLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="Learn how Loremaster protects your campaign data, what we collect, and how we handle audio recordings and session content."
  lastUpdated="September 5, 2026"
  breadcrumbLabel="Privacy Policy"
>
  <p>
    This Privacy Policy explains how Valfar and Sons, Inc. ("Valfar and Sons," "we," "us," or
    "our") collects, uses, discloses, and retains information when you use the Loremaster platform
    and related applications, websites, and services (collectively, the "Service").
  </p>
  <p>
    By using Loremaster, you agree to the collection and use of information as described in this
    Privacy Policy.
  </p>

  <h2>1) What Information We Collect</h2>
  <p>We collect information in the following categories:</p>

  <h3>A) Account Information</h3>
  <p>When you create an account, we may collect:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Name and/or username (if provided)</li>
    <li>Email address</li>
    <li>Authentication details (such as password hash for email/password logins)</li>
    <li>Login method (email/password or OAuth provider)</li>
    <li>Basic account metadata (account creation date, plan level)</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>B) Information from Third-Party Login Providers (OAuth)</h3>
  <p>
    If you choose to sign in using a third-party login method (such as Google or Discord), we may
    receive information from that provider, depending on what you authorize and what the provider
    makes available, such as:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Name and/or username</li>
    <li>Email address</li>
    <li>Profile image (if available)</li>
    <li>A unique identifier associated with your third-party account</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We use this information to create and authenticate your account and to help prevent fraud and
    abuse.
  </p>

  <h3>C) Campaign Data You Provide</h3>
  <p>
    Loremaster is designed to help you manage your campaigns. Depending on how you use the Service,
    we may collect and store:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Campaign names and descriptions</li>
    <li>Campaign notes and session notes</li>
    <li>Character names and related campaign information</li>
    <li>User-entered text, references, and materials you upload that relate to your campaign</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>D) Uploaded Audio Recordings</h3>
  <p>If you choose to upload audio, we may collect and store:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Audio recordings (including associated file metadata such as duration, time uploaded, and file size)</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Audio submitted for transcription may be processed using speaker identification
    (diarization) technology that analyzes vocal characteristics to distinguish between
    speakers. For details on how speaker identification data is handled, see
    <a href="#speaker-identification">Section 1H (Speaker Identification Processing)</a> below.
  </p>

  <h3>E) Transcripts</h3>
  <p>If you use transcription features, we may collect and store:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Transcripts generated from uploaded audio</li>
    <li>Transcripts you upload directly</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>F) AI Outputs</h3>
  <p>We may generate and store content created by our Service using AI processing, including:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Summaries</li>
    <li>Extracted entities (e.g., names, locations, items)</li>
    <li>Q&A responses</li>
    <li>Campaign insights or suggested content ("AI Outputs")</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    <strong>Important:</strong> AI Outputs may contain errors, omissions, or inaccuracies. You are
    responsible for reviewing AI Outputs before relying on them.
  </p>

  <h3>G) Usage and Technical Information</h3>
  <p>We may automatically collect:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Device and browser information</li>
    <li>IP address (and approximate location derived from IP)</li>
    <li>Log data (timestamps, pages visited, feature usage, errors/crash reports)</li>
    <li>Performance metrics (latency, feature reliability)</li>
    <li>Cookies or similar technologies (as needed for login sessions and basic functionality)</li>
  </ul>

  <h3 id="speaker-identification">H) Speaker Identification Processing</h3>
  <p>
    When you use transcription features, Loremaster may process uploaded audio using
    speaker identification (diarization) to generate speaker-labeled transcripts. This
    process analyzes vocal characteristics to distinguish between different speakers in
    a recording.
  </p>
  <p>
    Speaker identification data is retained as part of the transcript. For details on
    how long this data is kept and when it is deleted, see
    <a href="#speaker-id-retention">Speaker Identification Data Retention</a> below.
  </p>
  <p>
    Audio is sent to a third-party provider for processing. For details on which
    providers we use, see our <a href="/subprocessors">Subprocessors page</a>.
  </p>
  <p>
    You are responsible for obtaining consent from all speakers before uploading audio
    for transcription. For more on your consent obligations, see
    <a href="/terms#speaker-identification">Section 5.6 of our Terms of Service</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>2) How We Use Your Information</h2>
  <p>We use the information we collect for the following purposes:</p>

  <h3>A) Provide and Operate Loremaster</h3>
  <p>Including to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Create and manage your account</li>
    <li>Authenticate logins</li>
    <li>Store and organize campaign content</li>
    <li>Store and process uploaded audio</li>
    <li>Generate transcripts and AI Outputs</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>B) Improve Loremaster Functionality</h3>
  <p>Including to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Improve feature quality, accuracy, and reliability</li>
    <li>Diagnose bugs and service issues</li>
    <li>Develop new features</li>
    <li>Prevent abuse and enforce usage limits</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>C) Communications and Support</h3>
  <p>Including to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Respond to support requests</li>
    <li>Contact you about account and billing issues</li>
    <li>Send important service notices (e.g., changes, outages)</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    <strong>We do not sell your personal information.</strong> We use your data only as needed to
    provide and improve the Service.
  </p>

  <h2>3) AI Processing and Accuracy Disclaimer</h2>
  <p>Loremaster uses AI processing to help generate campaign-related functionality such as:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Summaries</li>
    <li>Entity extraction</li>
    <li>Question answering</li>
    <li>Transcript-based campaign insights</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    AI systems may produce outputs that are incorrect, incomplete, or misleading. We do not
    guarantee that AI Outputs are accurate or suitable for any specific purpose.
  </p>

  <h2>4) How Long We Retain Information</h2>
  <p>
    We retain information for as long as needed to provide the Service and operate our business,
    unless a longer retention period is required or permitted by law.
  </p>

  <h3>Audio Storage and Deletion</h3>
  <p>Audio recordings you upload are stored until you delete them.</p>
  <p>
    If you delete an audio recording from the Service, we will delete or de-identify it within a
    reasonable period of time, except where retention is required for legal, security, dispute
    resolution, or backup integrity purposes.
  </p>

  <h3>Other Stored Content</h3>
  <p>
    Campaign data, transcripts, and AI Outputs associated with your account are generally stored
    until you delete them or your account is closed.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Note:</strong> Deletion may not be immediate and may take time to fully propagate
    through our systems, including backups.
  </p>

  <h3 id="speaker-id-retention">Speaker Identification Data Retention</h3>
  <p>
    Speaker identification data generated during diarization is retained as part of
    the transcript. The related data that you control is retained as follows:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Audio recordings:</strong> retained until you delete them through the
      Service or request deletion by contacting us.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Transcripts (including speaker identification data and speaker labels):</strong>
      retained until you delete them through the Service or request data deletion.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Upon data deletion, all associated audio, transcripts, and speaker identification
    data are deleted, except where retention is required for legal compliance, dispute
    resolution, or backup integrity.
  </p>

  <h2>5) How We Share Information (Third Parties / Subprocessors)</h2>
  <p>
    We may share information with third parties only as needed to operate and improve Loremaster. For
    a list of third-party providers we use to operate Loremaster, see our
    <a href="/subprocessors">Subprocessors page</a>.
  </p>

  <h3>Business Transfers</h3>
  <p>
    If we are involved in a merger, acquisition, financing, reorganization, bankruptcy, dissolution,
    or sale of some or all of our assets, information we collect may be transferred as part of that
    transaction.
  </p>

  <h3>Legal, Safety, and Compliance Disclosures (Including DMCA)</h3>
  <p>We may disclose information if we believe in good faith that disclosure is necessary to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Comply with a legal obligation, court order, subpoena, or other lawful request</li>
    <li>Respond to valid intellectual property complaints (including DMCA notices)</li>
    <li>Protect the security or integrity of the Service</li>
    <li>Enforce our Terms of Service</li>
    <li>Protect the rights, property, or safety of Valfar and Sons, our users, or others</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="cookies">6) Cookies and Analytics</h2>
  <p>
    We use two kinds of cookies and similar technologies:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Strictly necessary cookies</strong> operate the Service, maintain login sessions, and
      remember your cookie choices. These are required for the Service to work and cannot be turned
      off.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Analytics cookies</strong> come from analytics tools (such as Google Analytics) that
      help us understand how users interact with the Service, such as which features are used most
      frequently and how the Service performs.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Analytics cookies are on by default. You can turn them off when you first visit, or at any time
    using the "Cookie Settings" link in the website footer. When you turn them off, we stop
    analytics and remove those cookies. Analytics cookies last up to two years. Our strictly
    necessary cookies remember your cookie choice for six months and your sign-in status for thirty
    days.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Do Not Track and Global Privacy Control.</strong> We treat a Global Privacy Control
    signal from your browser as a request to opt out of analytics cookies. We do not currently
    respond to browser "Do Not Track" signals.
  </p>

  <h2>7) Delete Your Data and Your Rights</h2>
  <p>
    Depending on where you live, you may have certain rights regarding your personal information.
  </p>
  <p>At a minimum, Loremaster supports the following requests:</p>

  <h3>A) Access and Update</h3>
  <p>
    You may access and update certain information through your account settings (where available).
  </p>

  <h3>B) Delete Your Account and Personal Data</h3>
  <p>You may request deletion of your account and associated personal data.</p>
  <p>
    You can also delete campaign content or uploaded audio through the Service where the feature is
    available.
  </p>
  <p><strong>Important:</strong> We may retain certain information for a limited period where necessary to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Comply with legal obligations</li>
    <li>Enforce agreements</li>
    <li>Prevent fraud or abuse</li>
    <li>Resolve disputes</li>
    <li>Maintain backups and security logs</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>C) How to Request Support</h3>
  <p>
    To request help with deleting your account or data, contact:
    <a href="mailto:support@valfarandsons.com">support@valfarandsons.com</a>
  </p>
  <p>We may need to verify your identity before completing certain requests.</p>

  <h2>8) Security</h2>
  <p>
    We take reasonable administrative, technical, and organizational measures designed to protect your
    information. However, no system can be guaranteed 100% secure, and we cannot guarantee absolute
    security.
  </p>

  <h2>9) Children's Privacy</h2>
  <p>
    Loremaster is not intended for individuals under 18. We do not knowingly collect personal
    information from children under 18.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you believe a minor has provided personal information to us, please contact
    <a href="mailto:support@valfarandsons.com">support@valfarandsons.com</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>10) International Users</h2>
  <p>
    If you access the Service from outside the United States, you understand that your information
    may be processed and stored in the United States or other locations where our service providers
    operate.
  </p>

  <h2>11) Changes to This Privacy Policy</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. If we make material changes, we may provide
    notice through the Service or by other reasonable means.
  </p>
  <p>
    Your continued use of the Service after the updated policy becomes effective means you accept the
    updated Privacy Policy.
  </p>

  <h2>12) Contact Us</h2>
  <p>
    If you have questions about this Privacy Policy or how we handle data, contact:
  </p>
  <p>
    Valfar and Sons, Inc.<br />
    Email: <a href="mailto:support@valfarandsons.com">support@valfarandsons.com</a>
  </p>

  <h2>Appendix A — Additional Rights for EEA/UK (GDPR Notice)</h2>
  <p>
    If you are located in the European Economic Area (EEA) or United Kingdom, you may have rights
    under applicable data protection law, including:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>The right to access, correct, or delete your personal data</li>
    <li>The right to object to or restrict certain processing</li>
    <li>The right to data portability</li>
    <li>The right to withdraw consent (where processing is based on consent)</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Where GDPR applies, we generally process personal data to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Provide the Service (performance of a contract)</li>
    <li>Operate, secure, and improve the Service (legitimate interests)</li>
    <li>Comply with legal obligations</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    To exercise GDPR rights, contact
    <a href="mailto:support@valfarandsons.com">support@valfarandsons.com</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Appendix B — California Privacy Notice (CPRA)</h2>
  <p>If you are a California resident, you may have the right to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Know what personal information we collect and how we use it</li>
    <li>Request deletion of personal information (subject to exceptions)</li>
    <li>Request correction of inaccurate information</li>
    <li>Not be discriminated against for exercising privacy rights</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We do not sell personal information as defined by California law.</p>
  <p>
    To submit a request, email
    <a href="mailto:support@valfarandsons.com">support@valfarandsons.com</a>.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
